📘
  🍇 Grapevine: a small ASP.NET / NestJS-style HTTP framework for Emojicode.
  The package's README has the API tables, the settings and the limits.

  Types:
    🍷  App         WebApplication: routes, middleware, controllers, settings, 🚀 to serve
    📨  Request     method, path, headers, query, route params, body, items bag
    📬  Response    status, headers, body, plus static result factories
    🆘  Problem     an RFC 9457 problem document, and the response that carries it
    🚧🔸🌐 HttpError  an error that carries a problem, for a handler to raise
    🧷  Binder      typed values from the body, the query, the route, a form, cookies and headers, and what is wrong with them
    🧬  Shape       what a body, a query or an answer is made of, declared once for the binder and the document
    🧬🔸📥  Read        what a binder read by a shape: the fields by their names
    🍪  Cookie      a cookie to set, with its attributes
    📎  FormFile    a file that came in a form: its name, its type, its bytes
    📁  Files       a file as a response, a file's media type, a client's name kept under a directory
    🗃  Static      a directory of static files to mount under a prefix
    🛂  Cors        which other origins may call the app, and with what
    🛡  Shield      the response headers that make a browser careful
    🚰  RateLimit   so many requests in a window for one client, and a 429 beyond
    🤐  Compression which answers are sent as gzip to a client that takes it
    🎖  Tokens      issues signed tokens (JWT, HS256) and checks them
    🎗  Checked     what a checked token claims, or why it was refused
    🛃  Guard       who may call a route, by its note and the request's bearer token
    🚿  Stream      what a streamed response writes its chunks to
    🗂  RouteGroup  prefixed route registration (MapGroup / @Controller)
    🛤  Route       what registering gives back: a pattern, a method, and notes for middleware to read
    🎛  Controller  protocol: ❗️ 🗺 group 🗂 registers the controller's routes
    💠  Value       a JSON value: read from a body or from text, asked, built, written
    🧾  Json        tiny JSON object writer
    📓  Notes       text under names: a dictionary of strings that does not leak
    📢  Logger      leveled lines, as text or JSON, with fields
    🎞  Wire tape   an in-memory connection, for tests that need to see real bytes
    📊  Gauge       for tests: what the program has allocated, and what serving a request left behind

  Handler:    🍇📨➡️📬🚧🚧🍉
  Middleware: 🍇📨🍇📨➡️📬🍉➡️📬🚧🚧🍉   (request, next) ➡️ response; next never raises
